<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116313" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρᾱσι</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρᾱσιν</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρας</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Men.
		</span></i>, v. infr.), Adv.: (old loc. pl. of
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span> (c)):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in season, in good time,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ὥρασιν ἵκοιτο,</span> as an
			imprecation, may he not come <i>in season,</i> i.e. <i>bad luck
				to him!</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				266.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMeretr.</u>
				10.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ὥρας σύ γε . . ἵκοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Pk.</u>
					131
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ὥρασ᾽ ἵκοισθε</span> (Dind.
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρας</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1037
			</span></i>(troch.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ μὴ ὥρασι</span> that
				fellow—<i>bad luck to him!</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				391
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ὥρασιν ἱκοίμην, εἰ</span>
			. . <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Salt.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ σύ γ᾽ εἰς ὥρας ἵκοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					53.7
				</span></i>
			 (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span> (C) <i><span class="en">
				B.
				1.4
			</span></i>).—For the form, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρασι,
				Ὀλυμπίασι.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
